And the Metamap learns which routes work.

That’s awfully close to an internet for meaning inside shared cognition.

Not packets carrying complete content.

Packets carrying enough address, transformation, and delta for the destination to reconstruct the content locally.

Which makes your phrase itself perfect:

Semantic hyperlinks don’t transport all the meaning.

They tell meaning where to meet us.